WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.868
-Finally, it is Tuesday.
It is time for "WeTweet."

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:03.868
Here we go, everybody.

00:00:03.868 --> 00:00:07.968
-♪ "WeTweet" ♪

00:00:08.801 --> 00:00:11.234
♪ "WeTweet" ♪

00:00:11.234 --> 00:00:12.901
-Welcome to "WeTweet."

00:00:12.901 --> 00:00:14.701
This is where we, as a group,

00:00:14.701 --> 00:00:18.534
decide something that we
should post on Twitter, okay?

00:00:18.534 --> 00:00:20.267
I'm going to show
you five different tweets,

00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:21.367
and we're all going to vote on

00:00:21.367 --> 00:00:23.334
whether you
like each one or not.

00:00:23.334 --> 00:00:25.100
You all have voting clickers
at your seats.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:26.467
Did you get them there?

00:00:26.467 --> 00:00:29.300
I can just tell by the confusion
that, yes, it is working.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:32.067
Now, you can all vote for --

00:00:32.067 --> 00:00:33.267
Why is everyone
looking left and right?

00:00:33.267 --> 00:00:34.367
You have them now, right?

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:36.267
Okay?

00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:38.100
Wow. Okay, here we go.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.801
You can all vote for...

00:00:40.801 --> 00:00:43.100
People are still
going like this.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.167
Either you have it or you don't.
Okay, here we go.

00:00:45.167 --> 00:00:46.634
You can vote for
all of them, okay?

00:00:46.634 --> 00:00:47.901
That's the fun of the game.

00:00:47.901 --> 00:00:49.734
You can vote for all of them,
whatever you want,

00:00:49.734 --> 00:00:51.367
and we'll see the results live.

00:00:51.367 --> 00:00:53.300
Or you can vote for
none of them,

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:54.601
if you don't feel like
doing this.

00:00:54.601 --> 00:00:56.901
You can just go,
"Jimmy, you do the work.

00:00:56.901 --> 00:00:59.133
I'm not doing the work for you.
Yeah."

00:00:59.133 --> 00:01:00.634
Roots, you have clickers,
as well.

00:01:00.634 --> 00:01:01.767
-Yep.
-Yes, we do.

00:01:01.767 --> 00:01:04.000
-How correct have you been,
Tariq, on these?

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:05.968
-Oh, I'm always spot on.

00:01:05.968 --> 00:01:08.067
-You know which one
is going to be tweeted.

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:09.634
-Absolutely. Yeah.

00:01:09.634 --> 00:01:11.400
-Quest?
-I'm 50/50.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:12.767
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:12.767 --> 00:01:14.634
-I know which ones they are,
but we didn't rehearse it,

00:01:14.634 --> 00:01:16.133
so The Roots do not know.

00:01:16.133 --> 00:01:17.601
And I think I know
which one it is, too,

00:01:17.601 --> 00:01:19.000
but I've been pretty good.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:20.100
I think I've nailed it.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.834
-Uh, not so much.

00:01:22.834 --> 00:01:24.300
-You have no idea which one --

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:26.167
what I'm voting for
or what I'm doing or --

00:01:26.167 --> 00:01:27.601
It's all -- It's private.

00:01:27.601 --> 00:01:30.367
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.367 --> 00:01:32.801
-Alright, whatever tweet
gets the most likes,

00:01:32.801 --> 00:01:34.567
we will tweet it out
live on the show,

00:01:34.567 --> 00:01:38.834
and you can all like it
and "WeTweet" it from home.

00:01:38.834 --> 00:01:41.100
Thank you.
It's a shared experience.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.267
You guys -- Are you guys ready
to have some fun?

00:01:43.267 --> 00:01:45.767
[ Cheers and applause ]
Alright, here we go.

00:01:45.767 --> 00:01:48.667
The first tweet is...

00:01:54.534 --> 00:01:57.667
Alright. Alright. Wow.
♪♪

00:01:57.667 --> 00:02:02.000
Uh...I like that,

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:06.334
but I feel like the audience is,
like, tepid on that one.

00:02:06.334 --> 00:02:09.200
The votes are in.
Let's see the results.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:11.400
Alright, there you go.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:14.400
It was, yeah, like almost 50/50,
but, yeah, it was a non-tweet.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.534
Here we go.
[ Sad tuba plays ]

00:02:15.534 --> 00:02:18.334
Thank you, Damon.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.334 --> 00:02:20.334
Alright, here's the next one.
The next one is...

00:02:25.701 --> 00:02:27.467
♪♪

00:02:27.467 --> 00:02:29.567
"You don't think
I can handle that?

00:02:30.901 --> 00:02:34.133
You don't think I can handle a
little bump and grind?"

00:02:38.467 --> 00:02:40.534
Let's see --
Let's see the results.

00:02:40.534 --> 00:02:41.534
Here we go.

00:02:41.534 --> 00:02:42.868
Oh, yeah, yeah.

00:02:42.868 --> 00:02:44.167
That's a goodie.
That's a good one.

00:02:44.167 --> 00:02:45.367
"Yeah, you don't trust me?

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:49.367
Come on. I can do it."

00:02:49.367 --> 00:02:51.167
Alright, next one here.

00:02:59.434 --> 00:03:02.601
♪♪

00:03:09.868 --> 00:03:10.968
Okay.

00:03:10.968 --> 00:03:12.701
Let's see the results
on that one.

00:03:12.701 --> 00:03:17.200
Yeah!
♪♪

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:20.434
You have to, right?
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:20.434 --> 00:03:21.667
You calling it right now?

00:03:21.667 --> 00:03:23.601
-No, I was wrong on that one.
-You were?

00:03:23.601 --> 00:03:25.400
-Yeah.
-Oh, wow. Interesting.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:26.868
I would be
a little disappointed.

00:03:26.868 --> 00:03:29.834
He has to do that, right?
Yeah. Next up.

00:03:36.801 --> 00:03:39.400
♪♪

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:40.968
Oh, don't -- You're playing
the theme wrong.

00:03:40.968 --> 00:03:43.834
